---
description: Resolve the requested retained-dictation outcome through owned capture provenance, exact acknowledged text and current draft authority.
budget: { maxTurns: 40 }
args:
  goal: string
returns: DictationResult
---
Work toward the actual requested dictation outcome. The focused investigation branch can find the owned thread, inspect relevant capture, segment, acknowledgment and draft evidence, and reconcile what text is genuinely retained. Choose investigations and further work from actual results and the user's requested scope, without treating a fixed pair of reads as proof of current state.

Use the installed dictation review branch when a real retained transcript needs the requested draft judgment. Preserve verbatim confirmed text, its source language and actual acknowledgment limits; provisional, conflicting, abandoned or unconfirmed segments are not permission to invent a continuation. A silence result does not create words. Retain the current draft revision and do not replace another draft or a later edit.

The decision branch can distinguish a read-only answer, an honest hold and a user-authorized private correction or separate alternative. Use the native finish boundary for any local stage and retain its actual receipt or refusal. Do not edit the draft, send a message or report a stage as completed without native evidence. Return the actual requested answer and any retained artifact.
